# GitHub reads this file and renders a "Cite this repository" box from it, so
# everything below is public the moment it is pushed.
#
# !! BEFORE RELEASE OR SUBMISSION !!
# The two orcid: lines are PLACEHOLDERS. 0000-0000-0000-0000 is not a real
# identifier, and GitHub will render it as a working link. Replace both with
# real ORCID iDs, or delete the orcid: lines - a missing field is honest, a
# zeroed one is not. Check date-released against the actual release date too.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Benson Increments Calculator"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free web calculator that estimates the standard enthalpy of
  formation of an organic molecule from Benson group increments. The user
  chooses the groups and corrections a molecule needs; the tool does the
  arithmetic and shows the working. Written for teaching, so it deliberately
  does not parse structures or decide which groups apply.
keywords:
  - thermochemistry
  - group additivity
  - Benson increments
  - enthalpy of formation
  - chemistry education
authors:
  - family-names: "Kumar"
    given-names: "Prashant"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # PLACEHOLDER - see note above
  - family-names: "Pohl"
    given-names: "Nicola L. B."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # PLACEHOLDER - see note above
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrashantKumarChem/Benson-Increments-Calculator"
url: "https://prashantkumarchem.github.io/Benson-Increments-Calculator/"
license: GPL-3.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Estimation of Heats of Formation of Organic Compounds by Additivity Methods"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Cohen"
        given-names: "N."
      - family-names: "Benson"
        given-names: "S. W."
    journal: "Chemical Reviews"
    year: 1993
    volume: 93
    issue: 7
    start: 2419
    end: 2438
    doi: "10.1021/cr00023a005"
    notes: "The source of the increment values used by this software."
